.TH "ROARK\-AGENT\-CONVERSATION\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-agent-conversation-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-agent\-conversation\-create \- Start a conversation with an agent
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark agent conversation create
\fIagent\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Starts a voice conversation (`modality: voice`) or chat (`modality: chat`) with this Roark\-hosted agent and returns its id right away. `channel: web` is a conversation in a browser on your site. Call this endpoint from your server, never the browser: it needs your API key. Give the page only `web.clientToken`; the web SDK spends it to join from one of `allowedOrigins` before `web.clientTokenExpiresAt`. Read it back with `GET /v1/conversation/{conversationId}` straight away: `PENDING` until the browser joins, `IN_PROGRESS`, then `ENDED`. One nobody joins ends without ever starting and is never billed. Starting a voice conversation needs `call:create`, a chat `chat:create`, and the agent a published version that takes that kind.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/agent/{agentId}/conversations
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIagent\-id\fR
The agent\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-modality\fR \fI<value>\fR
`voice` or `chat`. The agent must have that modality turned on. One of: voice, chat, call. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-channel\fR \fI<value>\fR
How it is reached. `web`: in a browser on one of `allowedOrigins`, joined with the web SDK. One of: web. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-allowed\-origins\fR \fI<value>\fR
The origins your page may join from, exactly as the browser sends them: https only (http on localhost for development), no paths or wildcards. Repeatable. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-token\-ttl\-seconds\fR \fI<value>\fR
How long the browser has to join, in seconds. Default 120. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark agent conversation create <agent\-id> \-\-modality <value> \-\-channel <value> \-\-allowed\-origins <value>
.fi
.RE
